and fragmented plant material. The samples were dried (24
h, 40 °C), the soil material was sieved (≤ 2 mm), and the
litter was shredded by use of a plant mill. Soil organic
matter (SOM) contents (assessed by loss of ignition; 430
°C, 4 h) of the soil samples were 26 - 74 g kg−1 under
oil-palm plantations and 85 - 207 g kg−1 under rainforest.
Organic matter contents of litter were 304 - 872 g kg−1

